# Spec — Generative UI Catalog (interface contract)

## 1. DSL schema (json-render.dev subset)

```ts
type DslNode =
  | { kind: "stack"; axis: "row" | "col"; gap?: number; children: DslNode[] }
  | { kind: "grid"; cols: number; gap?: number; children: DslNode[] }
  | { kind: "text"; value: string | DataRef; tone?: "default" | "muted" | "accent" | "danger" }
  | { kind: "value"; ref: DataRef; format?: ValueFormat }
  | { kind: "spark"; ref: DataRef; window: number }
  | { kind: "chip"; label: string | DataRef; intent?: "info" | "warn" | "ok" | "danger" }
  | { kind: "action"; label: string; dispatch: ActionRef; confirm?: ConfirmSpec }
  | { kind: "panel"; title?: string; children: DslNode[] }
  | { kind: "list"; ref: DataRef; item: DslNode; key: string }
  | { kind: "when"; ref: DataRef; eq?: unknown; lt?: number; gt?: number; then: DslNode; else?: DslNode }
  | { kind: "diagnostic"; reason: string };

type DataRef   = { path: string; mask?: "default" | "explicit" };
type ActionRef = { name: string; args?: Record<string, DataRef | Literal> };
type ValueFormat = "number" | "bytes" | "duration_ms" | "iso8601" | "percent";
type ConfirmSpec = { mode: "hold" | "drag" | "chord"; ms?: number };
```

**Invariants**
- No `kind: "html"`, no `kind: "script"`, no `kind: "fetch"`.
- `DataRef.path` is resolved against the masked accessor; raw access is impossible.
- `ActionRef.name` must be in the action allowlist or the node renders as `diagnostic`.

## 2. gRPC contract

See `design.md` §2.1. Wire format: project-standard 5-byte length-prefixed gRPC-Web.

**Frame ordering guarantee:** monotonically increasing `cursor`. Client treats out-of-order frames as a protocol error and reconnects.

**Heartbeat:** server emits at ≤5s interval. Client treats >12s silence as disconnect.

## 3. Mint request contract (gemma_brain internal)

Conforms to `mem://features/generative-ui/mint-prompt-scaffold`:

```text
CONTEXT: <one sentence operator scenario>
DATA SHAPE: <abstract, no UI nouns>
SIGNAL TO CONVEY: <what operator must know after looking>
ACTION TO AFFORD: <what operator must be able to do>
CONSTRAINTS: <3–5 hard constraints, ≥1 forbidden behavior>
TRADE-OFF VECTOR: <optimize X, sacrifice Y>
FORBIDDEN: any named UI pattern, any element resembling existing gallery entry
OUTPUT: json-render.dev DSL only
```

**Rejection rules:**
- Element metadata or spec strings containing tokens from the forbidden-names lexicon → reject, re-prompt with stricter constraints.
- Spec failing DSL schema → reject.
- Spec exceeding 200 nodes → reject.

## 4. Frontend surface contract

```ts
function useCatalogElement(surfaceKey: string): Element | undefined;
function renderElement(el: Element, ctx: RenderCtx): ReactNode;

interface RenderCtx {
  data: MaskedAccessor;       // honors mem://features/security-masking
  dispatch: ActionDispatcher; // allowlisted
  theme: ThemeTokens;         // semantic tokens only
  diagnostic: (msg: string) => void;
}
```

No component outside the interpreter constructs DSL nodes at runtime.

## 5. Observability

- Every applied frame logged with cursor + element ids to reasoning-audit.
- Interpreter diagnostics counted per element id; elements with high diagnostic rates are eligible for eviction.
- gRPC-Web diagnostics surface in the existing diagnostics panel (`mem://features/grpc-diagnostics`).

# Spec — Operator Console Topology (interface contract)

## 1. Network surface

| Endpoint | Transport | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `:50051` | gRPC-Web (HTTP/1.1, 5-byte framing) | Primary RPC and streams |
| `:50052` | gRPC-Web (HTTP/1.1, 5-byte framing) | Secondary / sharded RPC |
| `/sse/*`, `/ws/*` (via nginx) | SSE / WebSocket | High-frequency state sidecar |
| Qdrant `10.149.181.190:6334` | gRPC | Vector ops (backplane only, not client-reachable) |

All client traffic flows through nginx. The native client speaks only gRPC-Web + the SSE/WS sidecar.

## 2. gRPC contracts (delta)

### 2.1 ChatService (new)

```protobuf
service ChatService {
  rpc Send(SendRequest) returns (stream ChatFrame);
  rpc Approve(ApproveRequest) returns (ApproveResponse);
  rpc Cancel(CancelRequest) returns (CancelResponse);
}

message SendRequest {
  string conversation_id = 1;
  bytes  ui_messages = 2;       // JSON-encoded UIMessage[] (AI SDK shape)
  optional string persona_id = 3;
}

message ChatFrame {
  uint64 cursor = 1;
  oneof body {
    UIMessagePart part = 2;     // streamed AI SDK part (text/tool-call/tool-result/reasoning)
    StreamError   error = 3;
    Heartbeat     heartbeat = 4;
    StreamDone    done = 5;
  }
}

message UIMessagePart {
  string message_id = 1;
  string role = 2;              // "assistant" | "tool" | "system"
  string kind = 3;              // "text" | "tool-call" | "tool-result" | "reasoning"
  bytes  payload = 4;           // JSON bytes matching the AI SDK part shape
}
```

Wire format: project-standard gRPC-Web with 5-byte length-prefixed framing. The server re-encodes the AI SDK SSE stream into `ChatFrame` events; nothing about the AI SDK shape leaks past `payload`.

### 2.2 ReflectionService

Standard gRPC `ServerReflection` v1. Client bootstraps by listing services, fetching `FileDescriptorProto` blobs, and loading them into a `prost_reflect::DescriptorPool`. Pool is the single source of truth for decoding any RPC response into `serde_json::Value`.

## 3. Schema contract

```rust
// op-plugins side
#[derive(serde::Serialize, schemars::JsonSchema)]
pub struct DemoPluginState { /* ... */ }
```

```rust
// zeroclaw-gui side
let schema = schema_for!(DemoPluginState);   // Draft 2020-12
let value  = grpc::decode_to_json(dynamic);  // serde_json::Value
schema::render_value(ui, &schema, &value);
```

**Invariants:**
- Every plugin state struct derives `schemars::JsonSchema`.
- `schema::render_value` never panics; unknown constructs render a labeled diagnostic.
- Raw `pretty_json` fallback is allowed only inside an explicit diagnostic frame.

## 4. Chat inference contract (server, self-hosted)

Inference runs in `gemma_brain` on operator-owned hardware. `op-web` is the gRPC façade and tool dispatcher. There is **no** AI SDK provider, no `streamText` call, no `LOVABLE_API_KEY`, and no outbound call to any hosted AI gateway.

```rust
// op-web ChatService — sketch
async fn send(req: SendRequest) -> impl Stream<Item = ChatFrame> {
    let persona = personas.resolve(req.persona_id).await?;
    let tools   = registry.tools_for(&persona);
    let cursor  = cursor::start();

    // gemma_brain owns generation + tool-call planning.
    let mut model_stream = gemma_brain
        .chat(persona.system_prompt, req.ui_messages, &tools, /*max_steps=*/ 50)
        .await?;

    while let Some(part) = model_stream.next().await {
        match part {
            ModelPart::Text(t)        => yield ChatFrame::part(cursor.bump(), "text", t),
            ModelPart::ToolCall(c)    => yield ChatFrame::part(cursor.bump(), "tool-call", c),
            ModelPart::ToolResult(r)  => yield ChatFrame::part(cursor.bump(), "tool-result", r),
            ModelPart::Reasoning(r)   => yield ChatFrame::part(cursor.bump(), "reasoning", r),
        }
    }
    yield ChatFrame::done(cursor.bump());
}
```

**Rules:**
- All inference is local to operator infrastructure (`gemma_brain`). No external model calls.
- Tools are defined in Rust with `schemars` input schemas; each tool wraps an `op-plugins` RPC and runs server-side only.
- Mutating tools require approval; approval round-trips via `ChatService.Approve` before `execute` is called.
- Agent loop bounded at ≥50 steps; cancellable via `ChatService.Cancel`.
- Wire vocabulary mirrors AI SDK `UIMessage` part kinds (`text` / `tool-call` / `tool-result` / `reasoning`) so renderers stay portable — this is a wire-format choice, not a runtime dependency on the AI SDK.
- Structured tool outputs are JSON validated against the tool's declared `schemars` schema before being framed.

## 5. Native chat rendering contract

The egui chat view mirrors AI Elements semantics; it does not invent new primitives.

| AI Elements primitive | egui equivalent |
|---|---|
| `Conversation` + `ConversationContent` + `ConversationScrollButton` | `chat::view::transcript` with sticky-to-bottom |
| `Message` / `MessageContent` / `MessageResponse` | `chat::view::message` (role-styled, markdown-rendered) |
| `Tool` / `ToolHeader` / `ToolInput` / `ToolOutput` | `chat::view::tool_card` (input collapsed by default, including completed/error) |
| `PromptInput` / `PromptInputTextarea` / `PromptInputSubmit` | `chat::view::composer` (always-focused, status-aware submit) |
| `Shimmer` | `chat::view::thinking` ("Thinking…" while `submitted`) |

**Style invariants:**
- Assistant messages: no background bubble; render on the page surface.
- User messages: filled bubble with a deliberate high-contrast token pair from `theme.rs`.
- Identity glyph: domain-specific mark (`gemma_brain`), never `Sparkles`.
- Tool input/output cards stay collapsed by default in all states.

## 6. Conversation & storage contract

Per `chat-agent-ui-contract`, before any chat file is written:
- Ask **two separate** questions via `questions--ask_questions`: conversation shape (threaded vs. single) and storage (database / local / none).
- If threaded → real route: `/$threadId` (TanStack) or `/chat/:threadId` (Classic) for the React workspace, `Route::Chat(thread_id)` in `nav.rs` for native.
- If database-backed → Supabase tables scoped to `auth.uid()`, message rows keyed by DB-generated UUIDs (AI SDK `msg_...` IDs go into a separate `text` column if needed).
- If local-only → JSON file under XDG data dir (native) or `localStorage` (React workspace).

## 7. Observability

- Every `ChatFrame` cursor + tool call/result hash logged to the reasoning-audit pipeline (`mem://features/accountability/reasoning-audit`).
- gRPC-Web diagnostics surface in the existing diagnostics panel (`mem://features/grpc-diagnostics`).
- Per-tool latency + approval outcomes counted; surfaced in the management dashboards (`mem://features/infrastructure/management-dashboards`).

## 8. Removed surfaces

- `op-web::handlers::gemma`
- `op-web::handlers::ui_gallery`
- `op-web` routes `/api/gemma/*`
- rust-embed of Vite `dist/` in `op-web`
- Any Lovable AI Gateway provider helper (`createLovableAiGatewayProvider`, `ai-gateway.server.ts`)
- Any `/api/chat` or `supabase/functions/chat` route pointing at `ai.gateway.lovable.dev`
- `LOVABLE_API_KEY` from project secrets

CI gate must reject reintroduction of any of the above, including the strings `ai.gateway.lovable.dev`, `Lovable-API-Key`, `LOVABLE_API_KEY`, and `createLovableAiGatewayProvider`.

- Every plugin state struct derives `schemars::JsonSchema`.
- `schema::render_value` never panics; unknown constructs render a labeled diagnostic.
- Raw `pretty_json` fallback is allowed only inside an explicit diagnostic frame.

## 4. Chat inference contract (server, self-hosted)

Inference runs in `gemma_brain` on operator-owned hardware. `op-web` is the gRPC façade and tool dispatcher. There is **no** AI SDK provider, no `streamText` call, no `LOVABLE_API_KEY`, and no outbound call to any hosted AI gateway.

```rust
// op-web ChatService — sketch
async fn send(req: SendRequest) -> impl Stream<Item = ChatFrame> {
    let persona = personas.resolve(req.persona_id).await?;
    let tools   = registry.tools_for(&persona);
    let cursor  = cursor::start();

    // gemma_brain owns generation + tool-call planning.
    let mut model_stream = gemma_brain
        .chat(persona.system_prompt, req.ui_messages, &tools, /*max_steps=*/ 50)
        .await?;

    while let Some(part) = model_stream.next().await {
        match part {
            ModelPart::Text(t)        => yield ChatFrame::part(cursor.bump(), "text", t),
            ModelPart::ToolCall(c)    => yield ChatFrame::part(cursor.bump(), "tool-call", c),
            ModelPart::ToolResult(r)  => yield ChatFrame::part(cursor.bump(), "tool-result", r),
            ModelPart::Reasoning(r)   => yield ChatFrame::part(cursor.bump(), "reasoning", r),
        }
    }
    yield ChatFrame::done(cursor.bump());
}

