## 4. Chat inference contract (server, self-hosted)

`gemma_brain` handles routing, compliance tagging, and projection ownership. The chatbot model is **interchangeable** — `gemma_brain` routes chat requests to whichever model backend is configured. `op-web` is the gRPC façade and tool dispatcher. There is **no** AI SDK provider, no `streamText` call, no `LOVABLE_API_KEY`, and no outbound call to any hosted AI gateway.

```rust
// op-web ChatService — sketch
async fn send(req: SendRequest) -> impl Stream<Item = ChatFrame> {
    let persona = personas.resolve(req.persona_id).await?;
    let tools   = registry.tools_for(&persona);
    let cursor  = cursor::start();

    // gemma_brain routes to the configured (interchangeable) model backend.
    // It owns routing, compliance tags, and tool-call planning.
    let mut model_stream = gemma_brain
        .route_chat(persona.system_prompt, req.ui_messages, &tools, /*max_steps=*/ 50)
        .await?;

